      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Enoch Cox platted Darlington in 1836, laying the town’s first streets and setting its early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Darlington’s post office has been operating since 1837, a continuous link to the town’s early communication.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darlington%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Pennsylvania Railroad served Darlington from the late 1800s until the 1960s, leaving wood‑pile trestles still visible along State Road 47.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
